{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7799","id":5214608121,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNtCa-Q","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7799","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7799.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7799.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7799","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7799/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7799/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7799/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/e48c43cf82e62046fed6b7c945bf0386dd0ac0b7","number":7799,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(fleet-paperwork): create readback compares body, state and labels (#6901)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n`fleet-paperwork create`'s readback verified only the created issue's title and number. The README promises the comparison covers `(title, body, state)`, so a create whose body was dropped or mangled — or whose labels were never applied — reported `created+verified` and every downstream consumer treated it as complete.\n\nThis makes the code match the documented contract, and adds the labels that were sent.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `infra/fleet-paperwork/fleet_paperwork.py` — `cmd_create`'s readback now also compares:\n  - **body** against exactly what was sent (length + shape in the diagnostic),\n  - **state** against `open` (a freshly created issue),\n  - **labels** — every requested `--label` must appear in the readback; extra labels GitHub added are tolerated.\n- `infra/fleet-paperwork/README.md` — the verification bullet now names the label comparison.\n- `infra/fleet-paperwork/tests/test_fleet_paperwork.py` — new `TestCreateReadback` covering the failure modes and the passing cases.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\ncd infra/fleet-paperwork && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\nRan 36 tests — OK\n```\n\nOracle check: with the previous `fleet_paperwork.py` restored, the four failure-mode tests fail —\n\n```\nFAIL: test_closed_state_fails\nFAIL: test_dropped_body_fails\nFAIL: test_mangled_body_fails\nFAIL: test_missing_labels_fail\n```\n\n— and all 36 pass with the fix, so the tests detect the regression rather than merely passing.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Create readback compares at least body and state (and labels when labels were requested) against what was sent, dying on mismatch like the title check does.\n- [x] A unit test with a readback payload whose body differs proves the failure; a matching payload passes.\n- [x] Existing fleet-paperwork tests still pass.\n\nCloses #6901\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code state=pr_opened at=2026-11-08T19:55:00Z lane=7b47536b-c162-444c-be8a-3a9538cc4cb5 task=11300 -->\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https: